<title>ITALY: Economy defenceless if Italy misses EMU boat - Prodi.</title>
<headline>Economy defenceless if Italy misses EMU boat - Prodi.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Prime Minister Romano Prodi said on Friday Italy must be a founder member of the single European currency and warned that if it missed the EMU boat, the economy and the lira would be defenceless.</p>
<p>But Prodi told a congress of the Democratic Party of the Left (PDS) that the government was very close to reaching key financial targets laid out in the Maastricht Treaty.</p>
</text>
